md('labels/labeling_methodology.md','''# Label methodology — no training labels supplied

This release contains observations/reanalysis and derived measurements, a target catalogue, and a validation plan. It contains no random labels, no purported expert labels, and no trained model. The catalogue mandatory flag is a proposed baseline design policy, not an observation or independently validated medical standard.

1. Raw data: OSM objects, API reanalysis responses, unchanged DEM tiles. OSM is volunteered mapping; reanalysis is a model-derived reconstruction, not in-situ weather.
2. Derived features: lengths, spatial proximity, DEM profiles and local slope. Preserve algorithm/version, CRS, source identifier and uncertainty. Missing data stays missing. No tower distance is yet calculated.
3. Rule-derived candidate recommendations: define versioned rules with guidance citations, contextual conditions, thresholds, rationale and abstention. Obtain Sri Lankan clinical/outdoor expert approval before using numeric thresholds. Cold risk must consider wetness, wind, exposure duration and clothing; heat risk must include exertion and vulnerability. High temperature alone is not a clinical outcome. Snakebite prevention is not inferred from invented encounter observations. Terrain slope is not landslide risk. No universal numerical thresholds have been asserted in this package.
4. Independent ground truth: experts assess representative trip scenarios without seeing candidate rule outputs, record recommend/do-not-recommend/uncertain for each resource, evidence and confidence, then adjudicate disagreement. Recruit first-aid clinicians, local guides/rangers, hazard specialists and telecom experts. Collect consented field connectivity measurements separately; do not invent outage labels.

Keep sample_id, resource_id, candidate_label, rule_version, rule_evidence, reviewer_id, independent_label, confidence, adjudication, and provenance in a separate label table. Blanks mean unlabelled, never negative. Mandatory resources can be served through a reviewed policy outside the classifier.

Split by entire route and weather grid cell, plus time blocks and held-out regions. Knuckles, Riverston and Meemure overlap: the same OSM way must not appear in train and test. Deduplicate by osm_type/osm_id across regions. Related points and adjacent hours cannot be randomly split. Hold test experts/scenarios separate from rule development. Report multilabel precision/recall, macro and per-resource performance, safety-critical false negatives, calibration, abstention and confidence intervals; compare against a mandatory-only baseline and rule baseline.

Evaluation against the same rules that generated labels only measures rule imitation, not independent recommendation validity. State this explicitly in research claims. Prospective usability/coverage studies and blinded expert validation are required for novelty and safety claims.

Critical temporal leakage: the system recommends BEFORE connectivity loss. Historical realised weather is suitable for climatology/exploration and retrospective scenarios, but using future realised weather as a pre-trip feature leaks information. Collect archived forecasts with issue_time <= decision_time and their lead_time for deployment-like evaluation. Likewise a 2026 cell inventory must not be silently treated as 2021 coverage. Record current observed connectivity separately from predicted upcoming connectivity.
''')
md('metadata/manual_acquisition.md','''# Remaining official acquisition steps

* Existing `knuckles_trails.geojson`: not attached to this request. Place a copy in `raw/trails/user_original/`; hash and validate it without overwriting. Compare with newly collected candidates; preserve original identity and tags.
* OpenCelliD: https://opencellid.net/downloads.php — create your own account, obtain an API access token, enter it on the official page, choose Sri Lanka if a current export exists. Never commit tokens. Keep the exact exported file, checksum, access date and schema; check CC BY-SA 4.0 and attribution at https://docs.opencellid.org/docs/downloads/overview. Exports cover cells seen within the last 18 months; a missing country export may require authorised API lookups. Crop by AOI plus a justified buffer. Cell coordinates are estimated locations, not verified physical towers or signal measurements.
* Dialog https://dialog.lk/node/453 and Mobitel https://www.mobitel.lk/coverage — request dated, operator/technology-specific raster/vector coverage layers and written academic reuse/redistribution permission. TRCSL https://www.trc.gov.lk/ is the official regulator to ask for public coverage datasets. Do not scrape map tiles without permission. SLT fixed home 4G is a different service and cannot stand in for mobile coverage.
* NBRO/NBRI https://lrip.nbro.gov.lk/portal/apps/webappviewer/index.html?id=7524ad70c98e4124a6f4dfed6ea615fe and https://nbri.gov.lk/index.php?Itemid=208&id=38&lang=en&option=com_content&view=article — ask for Matale/Kandy and other relevant district susceptibility polygons/rasters, legend, CRS, version and licence. Obtain machine-readable data if possible. PDFs require georeferencing with control points, positional-error reporting, legend-preserving digitisation and independent validation; reference only until then. Do not treat susceptibility as event probability or risk without exposure/vulnerability.
* DMC https://www.dmc.gov.lk/hazard/hazard/Maps.html and https://www.dmc.gov.lk/hazard/hazard/Report.html — request licensed flood layers for the actual trail catchments. Available national profiles have limited basin coverage; lack of a polygon does not mean safe. Irrigation Department https://www.irrigation.gov.lk/web/index.php?Itemid=271&id=138&lang=en&option=com_content&view=article provides an official flood-map starting page. data.gov.lk returned a retrieval error; retry the catalogue manually.
* Meteorology https://was.meteo.gov.lk/api-docs — public CAP/RSS is key-free; JSON requires an X-API-Key obtained from the department. Ask for historical warnings, geometry, issuance/validity times and licence. The new site explicitly marks information provisional during development. Current RSS alone is not a historical hazard dataset.
* Safety content: use `raw/safety_sources/source_catalog.csv` official links. Obtain document-specific offline redistribution permission, or write original concise guidance reviewed by Sri Lankan clinicians and attributed to sources. IFRC 2025 guidelines are programme design evidence, not an already completed hiker manual. Seek park-specific wildlife, ranger and evacuation information from the relevant park/forest offices and verify contacts before use. Wildlife content is not yet sourced/validated.
* Visibility: not offered by the selected historical archive variables. Keep absent. Investigate the Open-Meteo Historical Forecast API https://open-meteo.com/en/docs/historical-forecast-api for issue-time-aware IFS forecasts and documented visibility availability; do not splice a different model silently into ERA5 data.
''')
md('README.md','''# Decentralized Hiking AI — research data release

Collected 2026-10-14 for a Sri Lankan university prototype that recommends offline resources before a hiker enters weak connectivity. This is a PARTIAL traceable data release, not a complete training dataset. No model trained and no training labels created.

## Areas and supplied trail file
Ten provisional AOIs: Knuckles (primary), Horton Plains, Sri Pada/Adam's Peak, Ella, Riverston, Meemure, Sinharaja, Pidurangala/Sigiriya, Namunukula and Haputale. See `metadata/study_areas.csv` for coordinates. These rectangles are investigator-selected collection extents, not authoritative park boundaries. Some overlap. The user's existing `knuckles_trails.geojson` was not supplied and has not been validated or replaced. New files explicitly say `candidate_paths`.

## What files mean
`raw/trails`: unchanged dated Geofabrik country PBF, checksum, separate regional extracts, hiking-relation metadata, saved Overpass queries and any successful raw responses. Country PBF is the smallest available Geofabrik subregion and supports reproducible fallback extraction. `processed/trails/*_candidate_paths.geojson` uses the dated PBF consistently. Raw regional GeoJSON extracts are derived subsets; the original bytes are in the PBF. Overpass responses represent different snapshots and must not be merged blindly.
`raw/weather`: original Open-Meteo API JSON for 2021–2025. `processed/weather`: hourly CSV with requested point and returned weather-cell coordinates, API downscaling elevation and explicit UTC timestamps. Five Knuckles points and one point per remaining AOI, selected provisionally across the collection boxes rather than from verified routes. Refine them using validated trail clusters and elevation strata. These are not 14 independent weather stations; shared cells and ERA5 forcing create dependence. Model explicitly selected: `era5_seamless`, combining ERA5-Land temperature/humidity with ERA5 atmospheric inputs. Mountain microclimate and rainfall extremes remain unresolved. Visibility is unavailable and absent, never invented.
`raw/elevation`: four unchanged Copernicus GLO-30 2021-release one-degree GeoTIFFs. This is a DSM (vegetation/building surface), not bare-earth ground truth. Horizontal WGS84, heights in metres relative to EGM2008. `processed/elevation`: profiles sampled at <=60 m with nearest raster elevation and a central-difference 3x3 local slope in degrees using geodesic pixel spacing. Gain/loss are sums along OSM node order; direction is arbitrary, no noise smoothing. Tree canopy and raster noise bias gain/loss, so compare 30/60/90 m sampling and smoothing before reporting route ascent. Rows at tile edges/nodata remain missing.
`raw/emergency`: factual national contacts and OSM mapped facilities. OSM facilities need verification of operation, hours, potable water and rescue capability. OSM spring is not potable-water evidence. Facility ways may be lines, not building polygons; use proper geometry reconstruction if needed. Emergency numbers do not enable calls without a reachable network.
`raw/hazards`, `raw/connectivity`, `raw/safety_sources`: source catalogues; downloaded public warning RSS is a current snapshot, not historical hazard observations. Copyright-restricted PDFs and operator coverage maps are linked rather than bundled. No spatial landslide/flood classes, measured signal values, or independently validated targets are supplied.

## Collection and provenance
See `metadata/dataset_sources.csv`, `licenses.csv`, `download_log.jsonl` (exact request URL, UTC access time, success/failure, bytes and SHA256), and `file_manifest.csv` for produced-file checksums. Source catalogues distinguish metadata-only sources from downloads. `data_dictionary.csv` and `final_table_design.csv` describe meanings, units and proposed joins. `processing_manifest.csv` maps processed outputs to raw inputs and algorithms.
OSM candidates include path/footway/track/steps/bridleway plus hiking-relation member ways. Preserve all tags, including name, sac_scale, incline, trail_visibility, foot, access and surface. Never infer verified hiking status from highway=path. Review private/no-access tags, official permits, route continuity and local guide knowledge. Hiking route relations may contain mixed ways, roles and missing members. PBF relation metadata is retained but complete ordered routes are not assembled.

## Joins and final table
Use stable typed OSM IDs (`way/123`) rather than names. Deduplicate shared ways across overlapping AOIs. Elevation profiles join by trail_id and point_index; weather joins use justified cell selection/interpolation and timestamps, preserving original cell ID, request coordinates and distance. Do not duplicate an hourly value as independent measurements at many nearby points. Transform to EPSG:32644 for metric spatial operations, or use WGS84 geodesics as these scripts do; do not measure distance in degrees.
Licensed hazards later join through point-in-polygon/raster sampling at valid dates with legend and resolution intact. Connectivity later uses operator/technology-aware coverage membership or estimated cell distance, with age and sampling uncertainty. Nearest mapped facility distance is a remoteness proxy, not evacuation time. Water points provide mapped proximity, not flow reliability or drinkability. Leave unavailable features and labels NULL and add missingness/provenance indicators. No final feature/label table has been fabricated.

## Reproduce
Python 3.11+; install `numpy`, `rasterio`, `pyproj`, `osmium` from `scripts/requirements.txt`. From this directory run `python scripts/download_weather.py`, `python scripts/download_elevation.py`, `python scripts/download_trails.py`, and `python scripts/download_reference.py`. The dated PBF URL is recorded in the log; download it to `raw/trails/sri-lanka-261012.osm.pbf` if reproducing from an empty folder. Run `python scripts/download_osm_snapshot.py`, `python scripts/extract_osm.py` and `python scripts/extract_connectivity_proxy.py`, then `python scripts/process_elevation.py`, `python scripts/build_documentation.py`, then `python scripts/prepare_dataset.py`. Existing raw files are overwritten by download scripts; run into a copied versioned directory to preserve this release. Fixed dates reproduce the requested interval, but provider reprocessing can change values; bundled checksums identify this exact release.

## Licensing and ethics
OSM © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0: https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/ . Preserve attribution and applicable database share-alike requirements. Weather CC BY 4.0, attribute Open-Meteo and ECMWF/Copernicus; free API is for non-commercial use, which is distinct from the data licence. https://open-meteo.com/en/terms . Copernicus GLO-30 uses its own free licence: follow https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/explore-data/data-collections/copernicus-contributing-missions/collections-description/COP-DEM . Original notice: © DLR e.V. 2010-2014 and © Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014-2018 provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and ESA; all rights reserved. Derived notice: produced using Copernicus WorldDEM-30 © DLR e.V. 2010-2014 and © Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014-2018 provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and ESA; all rights reserved.
There is no single blanket licence for this mixed archive. Source metadata is not permission to redistribute source documents. The downloaded CAP RSS declares Public Domain in its copyright field; this does not establish the licence for all other Department content. OpenCelliD future imports require CC BY-SA 4.0 attribution and applicable terms. Do not republish sensitive field tracks, identifiable hiker records or private infrastructure measurements without consent and privacy review.

## Readiness and next actions
Enough for Knuckles data-pipeline development and exploratory terrain/weather analysis if verified trail geometry is provided/reviewed. NOT sufficient to train or validate the intended connectivity-aware recommendation model. Major gaps: measured/datable connectivity or licensed coverage, independent recommendation labels, licensed spatial hazard layers, verified route access/support facilities, finished licensed safety content, issue-time-aware weather forecasts and visibility. See `metadata/manual_acquisition.md`, `labels/labeling_methodology.md`, `metadata/quality_report.json` and `collection_report.md`.
''')
